Hi Guilherme and Mollie,

If you want to include helper functions, like a new probability distribution, in an external file (e.g. "helper_functions.hpp"), you just need to #include it at the top of your .cpp between the call to TMB.hpp and your objective function. Our WHAM package <https://github.com/timjmiller/wham/tree/master/src> has a few examples where we store several probability distributions and other functions in "helper_functions.hpp".

#include <TMB.hpp>
#include "helper_functions.hpp"

template<class Type>
Type objective_function<Type>::operator() ()
{

Best,
Brian

